{"version":"1","id":"sitepen","handle":"sitepen","name":"SitePen","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1667134932/logos/sitepen","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-6.6564,"y":6.9328,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":300,"newest_post_at":"2023-07-10T20:55:24.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2011-09-01T18:21:03.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.026667,"listicle_ratio":0.03,"question_ratio":0.06,"avg_read_time":4.525896,"summary_length_avg":317.312925,"title_length_avg":42.996667,"title_length_var":324.089989,"tag_entropy":3.164752,"tag_diversity":0.296667,"top_tag_share":0.123333,"avg_upvotes":3.153333,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.113333,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.036959,"zero_engagement_share":0.846667,"viral_share":0.01,"posts_per_week":0.693022,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.65,"recency_skew":0.013514},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[2.0882,1.5588],"cadence_depth":[5.4559,-3.4853],"hype_variety":[6.1912,-0.2206],"title_style":[6.6765,6.6471]},"top_tags":[["general-programming",96],["javascript",89],["architecture",45],["typescript",42],["webdev",39],["tech-news",36],["testing",25],["react",11]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["TypeScript 4.4 Cheat Sheet","The Definitive TypeScript 5.0 Guide","Intro to HTML-first Frontend Frameworks"],"outlier":["Episode 17: Presentations, Vulnerability, and Solving Complex Problems with Justin Searls (Live at JSConf US)"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"IebLnBIBm","title":"Leveling-Up Your Dev Team","url":"https://www.sitepen.com/blog/leveling-up-your-dev-team","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/leveling-up-your-dev-team-ieblnbibm","summary":"SitePen Software projects succeed or fail based on the quality of the teams behind them. Expert developers can be hard to find. It's not enough to teach junior developers how to use a framework or tech stack. Good developers know why patterns are established and how to improve the project as it grows.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ed24fbe569005a356cb2861c51c780b6?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":15,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-10T20:55:24.000Z"},{"id":"ZwEkdxD51","title":"Redesigning Enterprise Apps Efficiently: The Bottom Up Approach","url":"https://www.sitepen.com/blog/redesigning-enterprise-apps-efficiently-the-bottom-up-approach","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/redesigning-enterprise-apps-efficiently-the-bottom-up-approach-zwekdxd51","summary":"A bottom-up redesign is a safe, efficient way to improve your product without being disruptive to product development or other long-term objectives. For large organizations, improving their user experience is not a question of intent, it\u2019s a matter of logistics. It is important not to focus too much on perfection.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d10315e1b1830ea11efbcc9ea7b777c0?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-05-19T20:04:20.000Z"},{"id":"UNyWxXQvB","title":"Getting Started with WebRTC","url":"https://www.sitepen.com/blog/getting-started-with-webrtc","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/getting-started-with-webrtc-unywxxqvb","summary":"A client-side web app can use the WebRTC API, which is built into modern browsers, to access a system\u2019s camera(s), start a video stream, and connect to a remote system. In the rest of this article I\u2019m going to give a high-level overview of how Web RTC works.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/75ac16fe748c9c96d1f6f06755be19e9?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-05-16T15:57:28.000Z"},{"id":"Eeq5Xa9ct","title":"The Definitive TypeScript 5.0 Guide","url":"https://www.sitepen.com/blog/update-the-definitive-typescript-guide","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-definitive-typescript-5-0-guide-eeq5xa9ct","summary":"The Definitive TypeScript 5.0 Guide - SitePen was first published October 2018. TypeScript is a superset of JavaScript, but with optional types, interfaces, generics, and more. The Definitive Guide provides one of the best overviews of the key features of TypeScript.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1681977660/7451ddf94175c34d9d46f436b073c93b","num_upvotes":115,"num_comments":7,"created_at":"2023-03-21T11:32:52.000Z"},{"id":"gGeW7U9K1","title":"Building a Serverless Chat Application with Supabase","url":"https://www.sitepen.com/blog/building-a-serverless-chat-application-with-supabase","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/building-a-serverless-chat-application-with-supabase-ggew7u9k1","summary":"Learn about serverless technology, explore Supabase as an open-source alternative to Firebase, and build a serverless chat application using TypeScript, React, and Mui.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6bc10a1daa2cc98a620b01e68c9b6402?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":15,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-14T09:12:40.000Z"},{"id":"mhfqFA113","title":"Using Redux-Saga to Write a Game Loop","url":"https://www.sitepen.com/blog/using-redux-saga-to-write-a-game-loop","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/using-redux-saga-to-write-a-game-loop-mhfqfa113","summary":"Learn how Redux-Saga can improve readability, coordination, and isolation of logic in React game development. Explore the use of Redux-Saga in a Blackjack game.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/8c8c3e689ca2e9cf47bd5554191b18c6?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-13T17:39:52.000Z"},{"id":"ljb9ntsK6","title":"Writing an Online Multiplayer Game for the Web and Native","url":"https://www.sitepen.com/blog/writing-an-online-multiplayer-game-for-the-web-and-native","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/writing-an-online-multiplayer-game-for-the-web-and-native-ljb9ntsk6","summary":"Milestone Mayhem is an online multiplayer game where players aim to complete their milestones before their opponents. It was developed using React Native, React Native Web, TypeScript, Expo, Supabase, and Redux Saga. The game loop in Milestone Mayhem is based on Redux Saga and uses sequential logic flow.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/871a88c122d2e80f522523b2e7b0c6fe?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":15,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-08T15:53:10.000Z"},{"id":"TgvBOefk4","title":"Design to Development: Bridging the Gap for a Successful Handoff","url":"https://www.sitepen.com/blog/design-to-development-bridging-the-gap-for-a-successful-handoff","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/design-to-development-bridging-the-gap-for-a-successful-handoff-tgvboefk4","summary":"Improving the handoff between design and development can be achieved through the implementation of a design system, creating interactive prototypes, using design hand-off tools, and maintaining communication between the two teams. These practices can lead to a more seamless and efficient process with benefits such as a consistent user experience, reduced time, and improved quality of the application.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/dfc3b49193706ebf1663154b45c408da?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-07T13:23:57.000Z"},{"id":"6QgGI2T8v","title":"Exploring the Creative Possibilities of Markov Chains for Text Generation","url":"https://www.sitepen.com/blog/exploring-the-creative-possibilities-of-markov-chains-for-text-generation","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/exploring-the-creative-possibilities-of-markov-chains-for-text-generation-6qggi2t8v","summary":"Explore the creative possibilities of Markov chains for text generation. Learn how Markov chains work, their applications, and how to use them for text generation.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ee93d0841704ff2717a5ad617bec7223?_a=AQAEufR","num